--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/4 key facts kept) ---
I read of more than two and a half million workers unemployed, and of the great South Wales coal dispute; and I hoped that at least a temporary arrangement would be made to permit the miners to return to work.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/5 key facts kept) ---
I am glad to have finished a week of work.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (4/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I paid Mrs. Turner her week's wages, spoke with young Mr. Fenn about remarks, reckoned up £39 19s. 9d. in hand, and went to the clerks' room of the Moorgate Fire and Life Assurance Company, paying out the staff wages on the company's.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that she was scrubbing an office, and found a five-pound note.
      📖 It foretells good news.

