--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (1/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day I pawned my late husband's watch to raise ten shillings, wherewith to buy bread, margarine, tea and a little bacon.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (4/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I balanced the quarterly ledger, spoke to Mr. Walter Thomas about a sour jib, and reckoned up £3 13s. 7d. in hand.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (0/5 key facts kept) ---
Sunday. To-day I went to church; and, after reading the Psalms for the morning service, and listening to a sermon upon the duties of the week, I went home and dined. In the afternoon I walked out, and came back in good time to supper and to read prayers. And so the week began and ended.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that Kate Nolan refused to lend her a sack of coals, and that, in consequence, she and Bert had a terrible quarrel.
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt he was an officer in a crack cavalry regiment.  Continuing the dream: He was inHyde Park, and the Queen and Prince Albert rode past; and he saluted, and they smiled and bowed.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas: He dreamt that he was reading Trollope in an easy-chair, and listening to the wireless talk about contemporary life and events.

